{
  "id": "completion/templates/01_dependent_member_type",
  "topic": "completion",
  "subtopic": "templates",
  "title": "Dependent member type",
  "summary": "A variable whose type is a member alias of a dependent specialization completes the members of the class the alias stands for",
  "prose": "The alias is resolved with the written template arguments substituted, so `Vec<Vec<T>>::value_type` lists the members of `Vec<T>` rather than nothing at all. An alias naming a reference (`Vec<Vec<T>>::reference`) lists the members of the class referred to, and `->` on a pointer to one lists the pointee's.",
  "status": "supported",
  "issues": [],
  "files": [
    {
      "path": "main.cpp",
      "text": "template <typename T>\nstruct Vec {\n    using value_type = T;\n    using reference = T&;\n    T* data;\n    int size() const;\n};\n\ntemplate <typename T>\nvoid bar() {\n    typename Vec<Vec<T>>::value_type v;\n    v.;\n}\n\ntemplate <typename T>\nvoid baz(typename Vec<Vec<T>>::reference r) {\n    r.;\n}\n\ntemplate <typename T>\nvoid qux() {\n    typename Vec<Vec<T>>::value_type* p;\n    p->;\n}\n",
